  "query_preview": "..Strong high pressure remains centered over Utah and\nsouthwest Wyoming this morning, keeping conditions dry with light\nwinds. Some scattered high clouds will continue to stream over the\narea with highs similar to or just slightly warmer than yesterday. \n\nThe ridge axis shifts over the Four Corners region tomorrow,\nbringing a bit of southerly flow over Utah and southwest Wyoming,\nwarming temperatures by just a couple of degrees, with some maxes\nin excess of 10F above seasonal normals. This will also open\nthings up for a rather weak storm system to move through the\nridge, bringing just enough moisture and instability for just a\nfew showers over the higher terrain late Monday into Tuesday.\n\nThe storm system will act to curb the warming trend, with maxes\nmaybe a degree or two less warm on Tuesday than what is expected\non Monday. Dry conditions are then expected for the remainder of\nthe upcoming work week with temperatures staying on the mild side.\nThere looks to be at least some potential for a stronger trough to\nimpact the area next weekend, but significant ensemble spread\nmakes details vague at this time.",
